  "sourceIssues": [
    "The summary table states 47 courses and 141 credit hours, but the semester plan adds up to 136 credit hours across 46 courses (counting each Project/Thesis alternative once). The domain core and domain elective headings elsewhere in the document use \"/137\".",
    "The domain elective heading states \"(21/137) 7 Courses\", the summary table states 5 domain electives (15 credits), the semester plan has 5 elective slots, and the elective tables list 20 courses.",
    "The General Education Requirement heading in this document reads \"BS - Software Engineering General Education Requirement (39/141)\", apparently copied from the BSSE document.",
    "AI-444 Fehm e Quran (semester IV) and AI-610 Professional Certification (semester VII) are numbered outside their semester's sequence. Stored as printed.",
    "Semester headings (\"Semester - I\" ...) are not present in the extracted text; semesters were assigned from each table's \"Total Credits for Semester - N\" line.",
    "AI-354 Digital Logic Design is 3 (2+1) here, while the computing core list in the same document says Digital Logic Design 4 (3+1). AI-553 Operating Systems is 3 (2+1) here, while the computing core list says 4 (3+1). Semester-plan values are stored.",
    "AI-353 is titled \"Applications of Information & Communication Technologies\" in the semester plan and \"Introduction to Information & Communication Technologies\" in the General Education list. Semester-plan title is stored.",
    "Semester VII/VIII offer Final Year (Capstone) Project or Thesis as alternatives; they are stored with a shared alternative group. Thesis is printed 3 (3+0) and the Project 3 (0+3).",
    "Elective slots AI-xxx have no official course code; they are stored as slots linked to their elective pool, not as courses. Slots are printed with total credits only (3)."
  ]
